  MANUAL unit 2 [minor] english / make your mind good, of the zealous, in the smiting of obstacles: "of the zealous" hangs loose in English, while Hindi takes manāyataḥ as the one for whom the mind is made good ("उत्साही के लिए"); translations disagree. Settle one reading and use it in both.
         suggested fix: Make Hindi and English agree on the role of manāyataḥ (the note allows a genitive or a participle on the addressee).
  MANUAL unit 2 [minor] english / vṛtra-tūrye "in the smiting of obstacles": The glossary says names stay names (Vṛtra). The draft reads vṛtra- as "obstacle" and says so in the note. This is probably right for the compound vṛtratūrya, but it is a deviation that needs a glossary decision.
         suggested fix: Add glossary entry: vṛtra-tūrya = smiting of obstacles / of Vṛtra (choose one) and use it in every chunk.
